WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:04.660
FedRAMP High is a baseline for cloud service offerings that support high-impact federal

00:00:04.660 --> 00:00:05.660
use cases.

00:00:05.660 --> 00:00:09.260
FedRAMP itself provides a standardized federal approach for security assessment,

00:00:09.260 --> 00:00:12.700
authorization support, and continuous monitoring of cloud services.

00:00:12.700 --> 00:00:16.980
High is used when the potential consequences of a security failure are severe enough that

00:00:16.980 --> 00:00:19.260
stronger expectations for control implementation,

00:00:19.260 --> 00:00:22.780
assessment evidence, resilience, and operations are appropriate.

00:00:22.780 --> 00:00:25.540
High is a risk and impact category, not a marketing label.

00:00:25.540 --> 00:00:27.780
It should not be selected because it sounds impressive,

00:00:27.780 --> 00:00:30.719
and it should not be treated as a simple upgrade over Moderate.

00:00:30.719 --> 00:00:34.560
A High baseline reflects the seriousness of the federal mission, data, dependency,

00:00:34.560 --> 00:00:36.640
and operational consequences involved.

00:00:36.640 --> 00:00:38.480
If the use case does not justify High,

00:00:38.480 --> 00:00:42.930
the extra complexity may create cost and confusion without improving the risk decision.

00:00:42.930 --> 00:00:43.960
Several pieces fit together.

00:00:43.960 --> 00:00:46.790
The baseline defines security control expectations.

00:00:46.790 --> 00:00:50.000
The cloud service offering defines the service boundary being assessed.

00:00:50.000 --> 00:00:54.350
The authorization package describes implementation, evidence, assessment results,

00:00:54.350 --> 00:00:56.480
known weaknesses, and ongoing monitoring.

00:00:56.480 --> 00:00:59.330
The agency risk decision remains a separate judgment.

00:00:59.330 --> 00:01:02.805
Actual security operation is the daily discipline that keeps the service protected after

00:01:02.805 --> 00:01:04.040
the paperwork is assembled.

00:01:04.040 --> 00:01:06.890
A High baseline does not guarantee perfect security.

00:01:06.890 --> 00:01:11.345
It creates a stronger structured basis for evaluating whether a cloud service is designed,

00:01:11.345 --> 00:01:14.435
operated, assessed, and monitored for high-impact federal use.

00:01:14.435 --> 00:01:18.000
The practical question is whether the provider can show a live system with mature

00:01:18.000 --> 00:01:18.800
controls,

00:01:18.800 --> 00:01:22.750
credible evidence, clear responsibility, and sustained operations that match the risk.
